{# Why the book exists at all. Cycle 026: this block and the NAT note below
   were the two comment blocks the render dropped -- the stanza-level tests all
   passed without them, which is how they went unnoticed for three cycles. #}
    /*
     * Named objects rather than bare CIDRs, so the generated grants the access
     * broker appends read the same way as the rules written here.
     */
    address-book {
        global {
{% for entry in addresses %}
{# The file introduces its per-tenant entries with this note. Anchored on the
   first of them rather than on a position, so adding an infrastructure address
   above cannot detach the comment from what it describes. #}
{% if entry.name == 'acme-hq' %}
            /*
             * Per-tenant objects. A tenant's sites are an address-set rather
             * than one prefix, because a tenant is not a site: acme has two,
             * attached two different ways, and both must reach acme's cloud.
             * Adding a third site is one line here, not a new policy.
             */
{% endif %}
            address {{ entry.name }} {{ entry.value }};
{% endfor %}
{% for group in address_groups %}
            address-set {{ group.name }} {
{% for member in group.members %}
                address {{ member }};
{% endfor %}
            }
{% endfor %}
        }
    }

{# The most important comment in the file, and the one a renderer is most
   likely to lose: it documents an ABSENCE. Nothing in the model implies "there
   is no NAT here", so nothing but this template can carry it, and nothing but
   a test can notice it going missing. #}
    /*
     * NAT is absent from this file, and that absence is load-bearing. The
     * entire premise of the lab is that the leaves and the firewall act on real
     * pod addresses; a source-nat rule here would translate them to the
     * firewall's own interface address and quietly make every ACL and policy
     * downstream meaningless while traffic still flowed. Junos does no NAT
     * unless told to, so there is nothing to disable -- but `make verify`
     * checks that no nat stanza has appeared.
     */

